     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults of 3,200 mg/day, and the usual inpatient ceiling is lower. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO QID** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO TID** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory regimen\n- **600 mg PO QID** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO QID** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, which may have been the intended figure, split into a different schedule\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg QID, tell me and add a note on the intent. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
