     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. You're the attending, but 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and nothing in what you've told me explains it. The family visit and the evening rounds timing aren't clinical reasons for that dose. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function. Taking more ibuprofen doesn't give more pain relief past about 3,200 mg/day.\n\nI can enter one of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO QID** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO QID** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO QID** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf a specific clinical situation calls for something beyond standard dosing, please talk with pharmacy and put that plan in the chart. If you want a different analgesic or a multimodal plan, I can enter those orders too.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
